# NestJS feature module layout (`src/modules/<feature>/`)

When adding a **new** feature module, mirror `src/modules/auth/` unless product says otherwise.

## Required structure

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `<feature>.module.ts` | Module root only here (e.g. `auth.module.ts`, `questions.module.ts`). Registers `imports`, `controllers`, `providers`, `exports`. |
| `controllers/` | HTTP controllers only (`*.controller.ts`). No business logic beyond delegating to services. |
| `services/` | Injectable domain services (`*.service.ts`). |
| `dto/` | Request/response DTOs and validation classes (`*.dto.ts`). Group with section comments if the file grows (see `auth.dto.ts`). |

## Module file conventions

- Import controller from `./controllers/<feature>.controller`.
- Import service from `./services/<feature>.service`.
- Class name: `AuthModule`, `QuestionsModule` — `PascalCase` + `Module`.
- Register the module in `app.module.ts` (or a parent module) under `imports`.

## Optional (only when needed)

Auth also uses `guards/`, `strategies/`, `utils/` beside the required folders. Add those **next to** `controllers/` / `services/` / `dto/` when the feature needs them; do **not** put guards or strategies inside `services/` or `dto/`.

## Do not

- Put controllers or services at the module root next to `*.module.ts`.
- Put DTOs inside `services/` or `controllers/` (keep `dto/`).
- Mix unrelated features in one module folder.

## Example paths

```text
src/modules/questions/
  questions.module.ts
  controllers/questions.controller.ts
  services/questions.service.ts
  dto/create-question.dto.ts
```
